# hostwait: the step port's card leg claims its arena ids and queues their fills, computes the host's own slots under the
# fills, and joins them where the card's offsets need the filled bytes (NvTier::issue_card_hold, CardTicket::finish;
# crates/gpu/src/host/step.rs serve_one). Before, hold_for_card joined the fills first and the host list ran after. The
# series path exists on the card leg only, which only gpu-glm5next attaches (a pinned arena: the Spark's default, the
# box with BLOOMERY_NVTIER_MEM=pinned). Qwen3.8 and V4.1 take experts_into_resident, which already computes a step's
# hits under the pending ticket, so their A/B is not this card's.
#
# Decomposition of the step [derived unless tagged]. GLM-5.3-Flash UD-Q4_K_XL, 42 routed layers, n_used 8, 15.2 MB an
# expert, host leg bytes a token 4,055 MB = 267 picks, h 29.6..31.4 ms at 129..137 GB/s, host fixed cost F 2.5..3.5 ms,
# card front 12.8..15.6 ms [measured: glmslots-ab.card:14-17]. So one host pick is 15.2 MB / 133 GB/s = 114 us and a host
# list call costs F / 42 = 60..83 us fixed. Shape of this card: A6000, BLOOMERY_NVTIER_MEM=pinned, BLOOMERY_HOST_ROOM=80G,
# BLOOMERY_NVTIER_BYTES=20G: the host segment holds about 55 % of the non-card picks [assumption: 80 GB / 15.2 MB = 5,263
# of 9,500 host experts (glmslots-ab.card:28); the plan line fixes it, see the condition], so n_h = 267 x 0.55 / 42 = 3.5
# host picks a layer. Fills a token f = 70 on 34 miss layers L = 42 (1 - exp(-f/42)) [assumption: f near the Spark
# plan's 62.9 (t4-glm-card-leg.card); L as les-plan.md's], 2.06 fills a missed layer.
#   host list a layer   n_h x 114 + 70 = 0.47 ms (2.5..4 picks: 0.36..0.53)
#   fill wall a layer   2.06 x 15.2 MB at QD 6 = 31 MB at 6.0 GB/s (the box drive: 5.67 / 6.48 GB/s at QD 4 / 8,
#                       tierengine.md:467) = 5.2 ms
#   card arena read     2.9 arena picks x 15.2 MB = 44 MB over PCIe at 18 GB/s (refill-decode.card:43-44's 17.9 MB a ms)
#                       = 2.4 ms a layer, after the join, the card entries being PCIe-bound on a discrete card
#   card front          13.7 / 42 = 0.33 ms
#   step before         34 x (0.33 + 5.2 + 0.47 + 2.4) + 8 x (0.33 + 0.47 + 2.4) = 311 ms
#   step after          34 x (0.33 + max(0.47, 5.2) + 2.4) + 8 x 3.2 = 295 ms: the host list is under the fill's shadow
# Gain g = L x host list = 34 x 0.47 = 16 ms, 311 / 295 - 1 = +5.4 % of decode tok/s; n_h 2.5..4, L 30..34 and T
# 235..310 ms give +3.5..+7.5 %. The T4 shape (the Spark, t4-glm-card-leg.card: 26 host picks a token, n_h 0.62) gives g = 32.6 x (0.62 x
# 114 + 70) = 4.7 ms of 245..315 ms = +1.5..+1.9 % at the box CPU's pick rate: inside the ruler, so this card is not
# asked at that shape; the Spark's own CPU rate is unmeasured.
# Resource timeline of a missed layer (the wall is a sum of phases; inside the fill phase it is one resource's max):
# host CPU 0.47 ms of compute (the pool), the reader threads asleep in O_DIRECT reads; NVMe 5.2 ms busy (the max of the
# fill phase); host DRAM 53 MB read by the list in 0.4 ms and 31 MB of DMA writes under it; card SMs 0.33 front, then the
# arena entries; PCIe 2.4 ms after the join. Before: 0.33 + (5.2 + 0.47) + 2.4. After: 0.33 + 5.2 + 2.4. The host list
# is the term under the NVMe shadow: it is worth 0.47 ms a missed layer, all of it.
# Flow levers read and not taken (report only): the card's read of the layer's hit slots (0.8 of 2.9 picks, 0.7 ms) could
# run under the fill with a two-stage signal, 1.5x this card's gain on a discrete card and about 0 on the Spark (167.8
# GB/s reads); the fill phase itself is 66 % of the layer, which is the lookahead's (les-plan.md C3), not this card's.
#
# The one term the derivation cannot close: the realized overlap, host compute that runs under a pending ticket without
# slowing the fill or the list (16 reader threads and the spinning pool share the cores; the NVMe DMA shares DRAM),
# read as step_hits_under_read_ns / step_miss_layers in the changed arm's nvtier record: 0.36..0.53 ms.
# Instrument check [measured: gate-gpu-glm5next-nvtier, real tier, this tree, the card arm's nvtier record: 9 positions,
# plan (b') with a 41.3 GB arena of 64 slots paging 166.3 GB, so the host segment is a few percent of the routed bytes]:
# step_miss_layers 300, step_fills 788, step_fill_wall_ns 2.056 s = 6.9 ms a missed layer, step_hits_under_read_ns
# 9.02 ms = 30 us a missed layer, card_ids 2405. The counter counts the host list under the pending ticket, and at that
# shape the fill wall it hides under is 230 times the list (n_h about 0.3): the overlap is real and small there, which is
# why this card's shape carries the host share in its condition.
# Ruler: sd 2.6 % (refill-decode.card's paged-tier scatter), 10 rounds, h = 2.44 %; the near edge +3.5 clears it.
# Wall [derived]: an arm is a load (60..120 s for 200 GB paged) + prompt + 1,024 x 0.3 s = 5 min; a round about 10 min;
# 10 rounds + a warm-up about 110 min: batch it into one sitting.
#
# Runner (the lead; every variable but the rounds inside BLOOMERY_BOX_ENV):
#   BLOOMERY_BOX_ENV='BLOOMERY_LEASE_CARD=docs/cards/hostwait.card BLOOMERY_GEN_CTX=3072 BLOOMERY_DECODE_N=1024 BLOOMERY_AB_LOAD=arm BLOOMERY_AB_WARMUP=1' \
#   BLOOMERY_AB_ROUNDS=10 just depth-gpu-glm5next \
#     bin:<base tree>/target/release/generate_glm5next:prose:512@BLOOMERY_NVTIER_MEM=pinned,BLOOMERY_HOST_ROOM=80G,BLOOMERY_NVTIER_BYTES=20G \
#     prose:512@BLOOMERY_NVTIER_MEM=pinned,BLOOMERY_HOST_ROOM=80G,BLOOMERY_NVTIER_BYTES=20G
kind: ab
question: does the card leg's host list, computed while the arena fills of the step's misses are in flight, shorten the
  GLM-5.3-Flash paged decode step, where the fill was joined first and the host list ran after it?
term: decode tok/s @ n=1024, prose 512 (the corpus's first 512 ids), ctx 3072, A6000, plan a with BLOOMERY_NVTIER_MEM=pinned,
  BLOOMERY_HOST_ROOM=80G, BLOOMERY_NVTIER_BYTES=20G, MTP off, one slot; this tree's generate_glm5next against main
  9338821a5's, (ours - base) / base, paired by round
unit: %
predict: +3.5..+7.5
rounds: 10
sd: 2.6 % refill-decode.card (rig-log 09-30#q38seed-ab, the paged tier's paired SD over 4 rounds), measured on Qwen3.8's
  paged decode; GLM-5.3's paged decode is unmeasured and may scatter more
condition: one lease; both builds with their Cargo.lock current; every arm a fresh process (BLOOMERY_AB_LOAD=arm), the
  order rotated each round, one warm-up round discarded; no [cpu-busy], [other-busy] or [cold] row and no Xid in either
  witness. Both arms' plan lines and nvtier budget= and paged= fields are equal, the plan names a paged plan with an
  arena whose host_experts bytes are 45..65 % of the bytes it does not hold on the card (else n_h left the derivation's
  band and the prediction is re-derived from n_h x 114 us, not read), both arms' nvtier records read card_leg=on with
  card_ids > 0, the decode fills (fills - union_fills) within 5 %, and the greedy tokens equal (the change moves no bit;
  the runner's tokens-differ line reads 0 of 10). Read beside the ratio, not judged: step_hits_under_read_ns over
  step_miss_layers in the changed arm (0 in the base arm, which never counts the card leg's host list), fill_ns over
  fills, and each arm's pp tok/s at P 512
decide-in: land the change on its owning gates (an express piece) and write the row to rig-log (decode tok/s both arms,
  the ratio and its interval, host list under the fill a missed layer, fills a token, the plan's host share)
decide-below: read step_hits_under_read_ns / step_miss_layers first. In 0.36..0.53 ms with a ratio under +3.5 %: the
  overlap costs the fill or the list something (reader threads against the pool's cores): price it with a doubling probe
  and pin the reader's threads before claiming the change. Under 0.36 ms: n_h or the pick rate is below paper, re-derive
  from the plan line and the nvtier record's host picks, and the ratio is no claim
decide-above: the host list was longer under the fill than paper (a slow first touch of the mapping on missed layers) or
  the base arm paid more serial wait than the model has (F larger): read the counter and the base arm's host fixed cost
  beside the ratio before the number is claimed as the overlap's
